#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""rgb-controller: event-driven OpenRGB profile switcher. No polling, 0% idle CPU.

Everything is driven by D-Bus signals, pidfd wakeups, inotify or one-shot timers.
When nothing happens the process sleeps in the GLib main loop (epoll).

AC power is a hard gate: on battery -> PROFILE_BATTERY and every other source is paused.
While plugged in, the FIRST source in PRIORITY that has an opinion wins:

  pin       manual override from the GUI / `rgbctl pin` (optionally expires)
  loading   desktop progress bars + terminal package jobs        -> PROFILE_LOADING
  gaming    `game-rgb start|stop|run` (Lutris hooks)             -> PROFILE_GAMING
  media     Spotify -> PROFILE_SPOTIFY, other players            -> PROFILE_OTHER_MEDIA (+ per-player rules)
  schedule  time windows ("Off from 23:30 to 07:00")             -> whatever the window says
  power     power-profiles-daemon mode: balanced/power-saver     -> PROFILE_DEFAULT / PROFILE_POWER_SAVER
                                        performance            -> PROFILE_PERFORMANCE
  (nothing has an opinion)                                       -> PROFILE_DEFAULT

Reorder or remove entries in PRIORITY to change the behaviour. Edit the CONFIG block below, or
(recommended) put overrides in ~/.config/rgb-controller/config.toml; the daemon watches that file
with inotify and applies changes instantly. The GUI writes that file for you.

Adding a trigger, e.g. "camera in use":

    class CameraSource(Source):
        name = "camera"
        def start(self):  ...subscribe to something, call self.ctl.schedule() on change
        def stop(self):   ...unsubscribe
        def wanted(self): return PROFILE_CAMERA if self.active else None

    SOURCES["camera"] = CameraSource      # then add "camera" to PRIORITY

External processes talk to the daemon over the session bus (org.rgbcontroller.Daemon):
Hold/Release, Pin/Unpin, Reevaluate, Reload, Status, Config, History and the signals
StateChanged / Log. Use the `rgbctl` and `game-rgb` helper scripts rather than calling it by hand.
"""

